l":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1457632?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/foolishimp","html_url":"https://github.com/foolishimp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foolishimp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foolishimp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foolishimp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foolishimp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foolishimp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foolishimp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foolishimp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foolishimp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foolishimp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":61596,"digest":"sha256:748c55fdedb9345ff9462228cf1169cb4edf4ce8f3b889fbf62aed5acc9fd3b6","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-15T02:08:03Z","updated_at":"2026-11-15T02:08:04Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/foolishimp/specification_methodology/releases/download/specification_methodology/v3.1.0-rc.2/stdo_toolchain-3.1.0rc2-py3-none-any.whl"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/foolishimp/specification_methodology/tarball/specification_methodology/v3.1.0-rc.2","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/foolishimp/specification_methodology/zipball/specification_methodology/v3.1.0-rc.2","body":"STDO 3.1.0-rc.2 fixes a Purpose Context omission at successor acceptance: W35 now supplies the predecessor-conservation obligation at `product_acceptance`, while preserving qualification, release and ordinary-work behavior. The source law, default frames and native workflow contracts are unchanged. RC1's guide corrections and runnable frame tests are preserved.\n\nThis normal release follows the repository's RC convention and publishes six separate Products with the same RC2 suffix: Specification Methodology, Purpose Context, STDO Skills, Representation Tools, STDO Representation and Axiom Indexer. Existing consumers retain their installed selection until they adopt this cut.\n\n- Native cut: `21a9d4b93c5adef1e84a369360a99176b98793c5`.\n- Derived Product source carrier: `4a7f7cdfcd724d6b2e47b3d790fa88030b70d84a`.\n- Native manifest SHA-256: `b691b0249c82ff39033ae636c4eaa0ab44bafee3732c79a227eb9409d53776c4`.\n- The cohort JSON asset binds all six Product identities, their exact dependencies, 225 companion archive members, asset digests, predecessor dispositions and independent assessment evidence.\n\nValidation includes 52 frame tests, 28 existing and eight new context controls, 80 assessed-package integration operations across both host layouts, manager installation and dependency checks, and 12 offline visual-browser checks. An actual independent Claude assessment supports six exact query subjects. Unknown boundary inputs refuse delivery. Release publication and public installation evidence are recorded separately from semantic assessment.\n\nThese are bounded query and release claims. Whole-method qualification, universal coverage, automatic host discovery, code correctness and human exact-cut acceptance are not asserted. Compression/source-re-entry limits and retained visual limitations are recorded in the assessment and cohort asset.\n\nUse the [method installation guide](https://github.com/foolishimp/specification_methodology/blob/4a7f7cdfcd724d6b2e47b3d790fa88030b70d84a/specification_methodology/v3/build_tenants/common/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md), [Skills getting started guide](https://github.com/foolishimp/specification_methodology/blob/4a7f7cdfcd724d6b2e47b3d790fa88030b70d84a/stdo_skills/GETTING_STARTED.md), and [RC2 migration notes](https://github.com/foolishimp/specification_methodology/blob/4a7f7cdfcd724d6b2e47b3d790fa88030b70d84a/releases/3.1.0-rc.2/MIGRATION.md). Download the six assets below; the manager runtime archive provides the declared macOS arm64 CPython 3.13 offline wheel set.\n"}